# Licensing

This repository is licensed per directory, not as a whole. Nothing here is
licensed by default — if a directory is not listed below, no rights are
granted in it.

## Functional Source License (FSL-1.1-ALv2)

Source-available under the Functional Source License, Version 1.1, with the
Apache License, Version 2.0 as the future license — the license Sentry ships
under (it calls it FSL-1.1-Apache-2.0; `FSL-1.1-ALv2` is the SPDX identifier
for the same text). Each directory carries its own copy of the full text:

- `apps/cli` — the published `demoman` package, which bundles the directories
  below into one FSL-1.1-ALv2 package
- `apps/mcp` — the MCP server an agent drives Demoman through
- `apps/runner` — the executor that drives Chromium and records a take
- `apps/studio` — the studio, where a take is edited and exported
- `packages/agent-bridge` — the run outcome types the MCP server and the
  executor share
- `packages/compositor`
- `packages/replay-engine`
- `packages/resolver`
- `packages/run-core`
- `packages/scene-schema`
- `packages/studio-protocol` — the messages the studio's pages and its server
  exchange

Any use other than a Competing Use is permitted: running it, reading it,
changing it, and using it inside your organisation. A Competing Use is making
it available to others in a commercial product or service that substitutes for
it, substitutes for a product or service the licensor offers using it, or
offers substantially the same functionality. Each version becomes
available under the Apache License, Version 2.0 two years after it is released.
The text in each directory's `LICENSE` is what binds; this paragraph only
summarises it.

Code by others that these directories bundle or ship keeps its own license;
the published package lists it in `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES`.

## All rights reserved

- `apps/docs` — the documentation's text and images.
- `brand/` — the marks and lockups.
- `scripts/` and `.github/` — the repository's own build, test and release
  tooling.
- Every file at the repository root other than this one.

"Demoman" and its logo are the licensor's marks. No license above grants any
right to use them, beyond what each license itself says.

